{
  "openapi": "3.0.1",
  "info": {
    "title": "Data360 API",
    "description": "The Data360 API provides programmatic access to the World Bank's Data360 catalog of indicators, datasets, and reference metadata.\n\n## How the documentation is organized\n\nThis specification follows a **layered documentation** model commonly used for complex catalog APIs:\n\n1. **Operation pages** (the *Try it out* section for each endpoint) keep request and response examples short and focused. They show the most common usage and link to the full schema for everything else.\n2. **Schema reference** (under `components/schemas`) contains the complete, authoritative field list for every response type. Use it to discover field names, types, and which fields are nullable.\n3. **Description prose** (this section, and the description block of each operation) explains cross-cutting concerns: query syntax, namespacing, pagination, and how the schemas relate to each other.\n\n## Top-level namespaces in the metadata document\n\nA single metadata document (returned by `/data360/searchv2` and `/data360/metadata`) is partitioned into several **namespaces**. The `series_description` namespace shown in the request examples is only one of them. The full list:\n\n| Namespace | Contents |\n| --- | --- |\n| *(root)* | Indexing fields: `id`, `idno`, `type`, `subtype`, `dsd_name`, `dsd_version`, `dsd_codelist`, `data_confidentiality_code`, `disaggregation_types`, `tags`, `@search.score`, etc. |\n| `metadata_information` | Document-level metadata: `title`, `version_statement`, `producers`. |\n| `series_description` | The bulk of the descriptive metadata for an indicator (definitions, methodology, references, topics, dimensions, sources, license, links, ref_country, time_periods, etc.). |\n| `additional` | Visualization hints (`visualization`, `metadata_link`). |\n| `disaggregation_codes` | Per-dimension codelist values. |\n\nThe `type` field at the document root is the discriminator: it can be `indicator`, `database`, `economy`, or other catalog object types. **This specification documents the `indicator` variant in detail**; other variants share the root fields but may populate different subsets of the namespaces.\n\n## Query syntax (OData-style)\n\nThe `/data360/searchv2` and `/data360/metadata` endpoints accept an OData-style query expression. Key constructs:\n\n- `$filter=<expr>` — Boolean expression to narrow the result set. Operators: `eq`, `ne`, `gt`, `lt`, `and`, `or`, `not`.\n- `$select=<csv>` — Comma-separated list of fields to project. Use slash-paths to reach nested fields: `series_description/idno`.\n- `$orderby=<field>` — Order results by a (possibly nested) field.\n- `any(t: <expr>)` — Quantifier for array fields. Example: `series_description/topics/any(t: t/name eq 'Health')`.\n- Slash-path navigation reaches into namespaces: `series_description/database_id`, `metadata_information/title`, etc.\n\n## Pagination\n\nAll list responses are capped at 1000 records per call. Use `top` (max page size) and `skip` (offset) on `/data360/searchv2`, and `skip` on `/data360/data`.\n",
